{"id":"7cd9013c-7675-4d58-ac2c-9fd417d82e36","object":"chat.completion","created":1793333241,"model":"deepseek-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"Check the course tests' expectations for the formatter budget before editing.\n\n```python\nprint(search_code(\"max_message_chars\", [\"tests\", \"deepinfer\"], 40))\n```\n</br>Search message related tests.Print matched lines with context by reading the test file names found.\n\n```python\nimport re\nhits = search_code(\"max_message_chars\", [\".\"], 40)\nprint(hits)\n```\n</br>Read the test file.Inspect the test file paths returned so I can read the relevant tests.\n\n```python\nprint(hits)\n```\n</br>Read files.\n\n<analysis>\nThe conversation is a coding task (not a chat for text conversion) — the instructions at the end ask for a \"conversation summarization\" but there is no existing summary text; I must produce one based on the whole transcript.\n\nLet me walk through the transcript:\n\n1. System prompt: describes tools available (list_files, search_code, read_file, read_range, read_symbol, write_file, replace_text, run_command, update_plan, recall, task_status, write_note, final_answer) with keyword args, dict returns, file hashes for edits, allowed imports list, and output rules (one fenced Python block per action, stop after it, no JSON wrappers).\n\n2. User message: the task — \"题目2：阅读真实源码，完成跨模块日志配置（1分）\". Details:\n   - Add env var `DEEPINFER_LOG_MAX_MESSAGE_CHARS` limiting diagnostic log message length, stats logs keep full.\n   - deepinfer/environ.py: config descriptor, None if unset, int parse >= 32, ValueError with var name for empty/unparsable/<32; cached; rearm/rearm_all support.\n   - deepinfer/logger.py: extend NewLineFormatter with keyword-only `max_message_chars` (None default, must be int >= 32, bool not int); truncate after %s substitution; keep prefix/traceback/stack_info; marker `...<omitted>...` (15 chars); budget 32 → head 9, tail 8; don't mutate record.msg/args/exc_info/stack_info; default handler uses config; no duplicate handlers on re-init; standalone formatter doesn't read env; `keep_full_message` must be exactly True.\n   - deepinfer/engine/stats_logger.py: add `extra={\"keep_full_message\": True}` to the queue-consuming logger call.\n   - Only these three files editable; required full reads of all three before first edit; must run baseline pytest before first write and final pytest after last write; generate run.log and patch.diff (three files), modified-source/ etc.\n   - Course execution contract: profile \"source\", editable three files, required_full_reads three files, verify_commands [[\"python\",\"-m\",\"pytest\",\"-q\"]], max_model_calls 20.\n   - Progress: phase=edit, baseline_done=1, remaining source changes for all three files, full reads registered with hashes, required mechanisms exposed (environ 3/3, logger 3/3, stats_logger 4/4), request_number 6.\n\n3. Assistant actions (in this transcript):\n   - First action: \"Read the head of logger.py\" with read_range(\"deepinfer/logger.py\", 1, 95).\n   - Then output shows executor feedback: read_range on environ.py 95-221 and logger.py 1-95/110-200, run_command python -m pytest -q returning rc=1, \"50 failed, 10 passed in 2.37s\" (baseline).\n   - Evidence blocks provided: environ.py lines 1-30, 31-94, 95-221 (EnvVar class, envs class, rearm/rearm_all); logger.py 1-110 (imports, NewLineFormatter with formatTime/format, _root_logger, _setup_logger, init_logger) and 110-174 (error line, excepthook, process mixins); stats_logger.py lines 20, 29, 342-344, 116-126 (_log_worker with `logger.info(m)`).\n   - Then multiple assistant turns attempted to call `search_code(\"max_message_chars\", ...)` but the outputs shown are just printed `hits` variables without actual results (the transcript shows \"Print matched lines...\" then `print(hits)`, etc., ending with `<analysis>` request — meaning those actions may not have returned results in the visible transcript).\n\nKey technical facts gathered from evidence:\n- environ.py: `_bool`, `_int`, `_float`, `_str` helpers; `_descriptors: dict[str, EnvVar[Any]] = {}`; `class EnvVar[T]` with `__slots__ = (\"name\", \"init\", \"lock\")`, `__init__(self, init)`, `__set_name__` registering into `_descriptors`, `__get__` that caches via `setattr(owner, name, value)` and wraps exceptions with `f\"{self.name}: {e}\"` (with TypeError re-raise fallback); factory methods `int(*, default=0)`, `float`, `bool`, `str`, `str_or_none()`, `int_or_none()`, `choice(...)`; `class envs` with sections (Platform, Runtime, Distributed Communication, MoE, Attention, MTP, Model Loading, Sampling, CUDA Graph, KV Cache Store, Structured Output, Scheduling, Logging, YoCo, Profiling & Debug, Multi-Modal); Logging section currently has DEEPINFER_LOGGING_INTERVAL_STEP, DEEPINFER_NCCL_MEMORY_SAMPLE_INTERVAL_STEPS, DEEPINFER_RINGBUFFER_WARNING_INTERVAL, DEEPINFER_GC_INTERVAL_STEP; `rearm(name)` and `rearm_all()` set descriptors back on class.\n- logger.py: imports datetime, logging, multiprocessing, os, sys, threading, time, ForkProcess/SpawnProcess, BaseProcess, TracebackType; `_FORMAT = \"[%(levelname)s %(asctime)s %(filename)s:%(lineno)d] %(message)s\"`; `_DATE_FORMAT = \"%m-%d %H:%M:%S\"`; `_LEVEL_COLORS`, `_COLOR_RESET`; NewLineFormatter with `__init__(fmt, datefmt=None, high_precision=False, use_color=False)`, `formatTime`, `format` (calls super().format, newline prefixing using record.message, color); `_root_logger = logging.getLogger(\"deepinfer\")`, `_default_handler = None`, `_setup_logger()` adds StreamHandler once, sets fmt via NewLineFormatter, propagate False; `_setup_logger()` called at import; `init_logger(name)`.\n- stats_logger.py: `from deepinfer.logger import init_logger` (line 20), `logger = init_logger(__name__)` (line 29), `_log_worker(q)` (lines 116-126) doing `for m in msgs: logger.info(m)` inside try/except with traceback.print_exc(), and `_emit_logs(self, msgs)` (342-344) doing `self._log_queue.put(msgs)`.\n\nPlan state: [{\"title\": \"Read required source files\", \"status\": \"doing\"}, {\"title\": \"Run baseline pytest\", \"status\": \"todo\"}, {\"title\": \"Edit environ.py, logger.py, stats_logger.py\", \"status\": \"todo\"}, {\"title\": \"Run final pytest and produce artifacts\", \"status\": \"todo\"}]. Note: baseline was actually run (baseline_done=1) although plan still says todo — the progress said baseline_done=1 and \"Do not reset a successful plan or repeat completed baseline checks.\"\n\nErrors: baseline pytest rc=1 with test \"test_invalid_budget[64] - TypeError: New...\" — expected since feature missing. Also earlier noted potential errors discarded.\n\nPending: perform the three file edits, verify with tests, produce run.log and patch.diff artifacts, final_answer.\n\nI should also record the planned code designs in the summary since they're the key next step:\n- environ.py: add `int_or_none_min` factory and `DEEPINFER_LOG_MAX_MESSAGE_CHARS = EnvVar.int_or_none_min(32)` in Logging section.\n- logger.py: keyword-only max_message_chars with validation; `_TRUNCATION_MARKER = \"...<omitted>...\"`; `_truncate_message`; `_copy_record_with_message` using `logging.makeLogRecord`; `_setup_logger` passes `max_message_chars=envs.DEEPINFER_LOG_MAX_MESSAGE_CHARS`.\n- stats_logger.py: `logger.info(m, extra={\"keep_full_message\": True})`.\n\nLet me write the summary with all sections.\n</analysis>\n\n<summary>\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user's task is 题目2 (Problem 2) of a course: read real DeepInfer source (fixed commit `774ce244b87cc0eb8d4b94ab9f5de2ab22049f01`) and implement a cross-module logging feature, changing exactly three files:\n   - `deepinfer/environ.py`: add centralized config attribute `DEEPINFER_LOG_MAX_MESSAGE_CHARS` using the existing descriptor/caching mechanism. Unset → `None` (unlimited); set → parsed with Python `int`, must be >= 32; empty string, unparsable value, or value < 32 must raise `ValueError` whose message contains the variable name. Value cached after first access (os.environ changes alone must not change it); only `rearm(name)` / `rearm_all()` re-resolve. Re-running default log init applies the then-current (cached) value to a new formatter; existing formatters keep their old budget.\n   - `deepinfer/logger.py`: extend `NewLineFormatter` with keyword-only parameter `max_message_chars` (default `None` = unlimited; otherwise must be an int >= 32, `bool` does not count as int, else `ValueError`). Truncation happens after `%s` arg substitution; only the message body is limited (prefix/timestamps/exc_info/stack_info unaffected). Use `len` and slicing; marker `...<omitted>...` (15 chars) counts toward budget; remaining space = budget − marker length, head keeps ceil half, tail keeps the rest (budget 32 → head 9, tail 8, marker 15). Preserve multi-line prefixing, time precision, colors, exception handling. Must not rewrite shared record's `msg`, `args`, `exc_info`, `stack_info`; the same record later given to a full handler must keep the full message. Default handler uses the centralized config; repeated init must not add duplicate handlers; a standalone formatter with no new arg stays unlimited and must not read env itself. If record attribute `keep_full_message` is exactly `True`, keep full message (`1`, strings etc. do not count).\n   - `deepinfer/engine/stats_logger.py`: in the real log-queue consumer, attach `extra={\"keep_full_message\": True}` to every stats message; keep existing queue, batch ordering, end signal, sleeping and exception handling intact.\n   Process/verification requirements: only the three files may be modified (plus run artifacts); must run full `python -m pytest -q` once before the first edit (baseline; expected to fail) and once after the last edit (must fully pass); generate `run.log` and `patch.diff` containing the three files; modified sources saved in `modified-source/`; do not modify tests, `pytest.ini`, `.course/`, dependencies or other business files; do not add CLI args. Course contract: profile \"source\", editable = the three files, required_full_reads = the three files, verify_commands = `[[\"python\",\"-m\",\"pytest\",\"-q\"]]`, max_model_calls 20.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Python non-data descriptor `EnvVar[T]` with `__slots__`, `__set_name__` registering into module-level `_descriptors`, `__get__` caching via `setattr(owner, name, value)` and exception wrapping `f\"{self.name}: {e}\"`.\n   - Existing factory methods: `int(*, default=0)`, `float`, `bool`, `str`, `str_or_none()`, `int_or_none()`, `choice(...)` — new config should be added as a new factory (e.g. min-bounded int-or-none) plus a class attribute in the `# -- Logging --` section.\n   - Refresh functions `rearm(name)` and `rearm_all()` re-install descriptors.\n   - `logging.Formatter` subclass `NewLineFormatter`: `formatTime` (microsecond mode), `format` (calls `super().format(record)`, multi-line continuation prefixing via `record.message`, ANSI color by level).\n   - `_setup_logger()` singleton `_default_handler` (StreamHandler on stdout, level INFO), `init_logger(name)` propagate logic.\n   - Non-mutating record handling: `logging.makeLogRecord(record.__dict__)` clone for truncation; `getattr(record, \"keep_full_message\", None) is True` identity check.\n   - Truncation arithmetic: `remaining = max_chars - len(\"...<omitted>...\")`; `head = (remaining + 1) // 2`; `tail = remaining - head`.\n   - Stats logger uses `queue.SimpleQueue` + `_log_worker` thread doing `logger.info(m)`; `extra` dict attaches attributes to LogRecord.\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - `deepinfer/environ.py` (hash `fe2c531989c419f0b51b169a07f5ed826dcec7f95c0c5bc3a351805923c4f218`)\n     - Imports: `from __future__ import annotations`, `os`, `threading`, `Callable`, `timedelta`, `Any`; helpers `_bool`, `_int`, `_float`, `_str`; `DEFAULT_PREFILL_MAX_SUM_SEQLEN_K = 2**30`; `_descriptors: dict[str, EnvVar[Any]] = {}`.\n     - `class EnvVar[T]` with `__slots__ = (\"name\", \"init\", \"lock\")`; `__get__` wraps exceptions as `type(e)(f\"{self.name}: {e}\")`.\n     - Factories including `int_or_none()`: `return EnvVar(lambda v: int(v) if v is not None else None)`.\n     - `class envs` sections; `# -- Logging --` currently:\n       ```python\n       DEEPINFER_LOGGING_INTERVAL_STEP = EnvVar.int(default=100)\n       DEEPINFER_NCCL_MEMORY_SAMPLE_INTERVAL_STEPS = EnvVar.int(default=1000)\n       DEEPINFER_RINGBUFFER_WARNING_INTERVAL = EnvVar.int(default=60)\n       DEEPINFER_GC_INTERVAL_STEP = EnvVar.int(default=1000)\n       ```\n     - `rearm(name)` / `rearm_all()` at end.\n     - Planned edit: add factory\n       ```python\n       @staticmethod\n       def int_or_none_min(min_value: int) -> EnvVar[int | None]:\n           def _init(v: str | None) -> int | None:\n               if v is None:\n                   return None\n               value = int(v)\n               if value < min_value:\n                   raise ValueError(f\"{value}, must be >= {min_value}\")\n               return value\n           return EnvVar(_init)\n       ```\n       and `DEEPINFER_LOG_MAX_MESSAGE_CHARS = EnvVar.int_or_none_min(32)` in the Logging section.\n   - `deepinfer/logger.py` (hash `5b8f8d9947de692353609c1fc2851097d24f9b6ba6004dce1dbfa394dc6d3ec8`)\n     - `_FORMAT = \"[%(levelname)s %(asctime)s %(filename)s:%(lineno)d] %(message)s\"`, `_DATE_FORMAT = \"%m-%d %H:%M:%S\"`, `_LEVEL_COLORS`, `_COLOR_RESET`.\n     - `class NewLineFormatter(logging.Formatter)`:\n       ```python\n       def __init__(self, fmt, datefmt=None, high_precision=False, use_color=False) -> None:\n           super().__init__(fmt, datefmt)\n           self.high_precision = high_precision\n           self.use_color = use_color\n       ...\n       def format(self, record):\n           msg = super().format(record)\n           if \"\\n\" in msg and record.message:\n               prefix = msg[: msg.find(record.message)]\n               msg = msg.replace(\"\\n\", \"\\n\" + prefix)\n           if self.use_color:\n               color = _LEVEL_COLORS.get(record.levelno)\n               if color:\n                   msg = f\"{color}{msg}{_COLOR_RESET}\"\n           return msg\n       ```\n     - `_root_logger = logging.getLogger(\"deepinfer\")`, `_default_handler = None`, `_setup_logger()` (creates handler once, then always re-sets `fmt = NewLineFormatter(_FORMAT, datefmt=_DATE_FORMAT, use_color=sys.stdout.isatty())`), module-level `_setup_logger()` call, `init_logger(name)`.\n     - Planned edits: keyword-only `max_message_chars` with validation; `_TRUNCATION_MARKER = \"...<omitted>...\"`; `_truncate_message(message, max_chars)`; clone helper using `logging.makeLogRecord(record.__dict__)` then `clone.msg = truncated`, `clone.args = ()`; guard `getattr(record, \"keep_full_message\", None) is not True`; `_setup_logger` passes `max_message_chars=envs.DEEPINFER_LOG_MAX_MESSAGE_CHARS` (import `from deepinfer.environ import envs` — no circular import since environ only uses stdlib).\n   - `deepinfer/engine/stats_logger.py` (hash `9ef93c3930d6dd8d889d4ba69558a85459c2210ae0714d5073c3b4328c8e7cb9`)\n     - Line 20 `from deepinfer.logger import init_logger`; line 29 `logger = init_logger(__name__)`.\n     - Consumer:\n       ```python\n       def _log_worker(q: queue.SimpleQueue[list[str] | None]) -> None:\n           need_sleep = True\n           for msgs in iter(q.get, None):\n               try:\n                   if need_sleep:\n                       time.sleep((dist.get_rank() % 8) * 0.005)\n                   for m in msgs:\n                       logger.info(m)\n                   need_sleep = q.empty()\n               except Exception:\n                   traceback.print_exc()\n       ```\n     - `_emit_logs(self, msgs)` → `self._log_queue.put(msgs)`.\n     - Planned edit: `logger.info(m, extra={\"keep_full_message\": True})`.\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - Baseline `python -m pytest -q` returned `rc=1`, \"50 failed, 10 passed in 2.37s\", e.g. `test_invalid_budget[64] - TypeError: New...` — expected because `NewLineFormatter` does not yet accept `max_message_chars`; this baseline run satisfies the required initial test (baseline_done=1) and must not be repeated.\n   - Earlier tool attempts to gather test expectations via `search_code`/`print(hits)` did not yield visible results in this transcript; no evidence of the exact test cases for invalid budgets, so the implementation should follow the written spec strictly (non-bool int >= 32 accepted, everything else `ValueError`).\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Confirmed the descriptor caching/wrapping mechanism so the new config gets the variable name prefixed automatically and honors `rearm`.\n   - Chose a non-mutating truncation strategy (clone via `logging.makeLogRecord`) so other handlers on the same LogRecord still see the complete message and the original record's `msg`/`args`/`exc_info`/`stack_info` are preserved.\n   - Confirmed truncation must occur before multi-line prefixing so prefixes/colors are preserved, and that `keep_full_message` must be checked with `is True`.\n   - Located the exact stats queue consumer (`_log_worker` → `logger.info(m)`) as the single place to add the `extra` kwarg.\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - The single large task message \"New task: # 题目2：阅读真实源码，完成跨模块日志配置（1分）\" including: the feature description (`DEEPINFER_LOG_MAX_MESSAGE_CHARS`, e.g. 64 truncates diagnostic messages while stats logs stay full; unset = unchanged), section 1 配置读取与刷新 (attribute in `deepinfer/environ.py` following existing descriptor read/cache; None when unset; int parse >= 32; `ValueError` containing variable name for empty/unparsable/<32; cached after first access; only rearm/rearm_all re-resolve; re-running default log init applies the then-current value to the new formatter; old formatters keep old budget), section 2 普通日志的长度预算 (keyword-only `max_message_chars`; None default; int >= 32, bool not int, else `ValueError`; truncate after `%s` substitution; prefix/traceback/stack_info excluded; `len` + slicing, count CJK/emoji/newlines; marker `...<omitted>...` counts in budget; budget−marker split ceil head/rest tail, e.g. 32 → 9 head, 15 marker, 8 tail; preserve multi-line prefix, time precision, colors, exception handling; must not rewrite `msg`/`args`/`exc_info`/`stack_info`; same record later to full handler keeps full message; default handler uses centralized config; repeated init must not add handlers; standalone formatter without the new arg is unlimited and must not read env; `keep_full_message` exactly `True` keeps full message), section 3 统计日志的完整输出 (find the real queue consumer in `deepinfer/engine/stats_logger.py`; attach `keep_full_message=True` via logging `extra`; keep queue, batch order, end signal, waiting and exception handling; no direct printing/queue clearing/stats rewrite), the table of three editable files with required reading ranges, the reading/context requirements (one full `file_read` per file before first write; chunk by complete class/function; optional `context_note` events 20–3000 chars sourced from real source before modification decisions; test evaluation does not score by reading volume), the `read_source.py` tool description and JSON output rules, 修改范围与开发记录 (only three files, all three must change; keep existing env items, descriptor members and refresh functions; descriptor may add helper factory methods; logger may add stdlib imports/helpers; stats module only adjust the existing consumer's log call; do not modify other business files, deps, course tools, `pytest.ini`, `.course/`; each write must log full `file_write.content`; do not pre-plant correct patches in the agent; run full `python -m pytest -q` once before first modification and once after last modification, final must pass; generate `run.log` and full `patch.diff` with the three files in the startup directory; no new agent CLI args), 自测与得分 (prepare workspace per README section 3, run `eval_deepinfer.py`; max 20 real requests, ≤32,000 chars per full request body, 1800 s default limit; independent checks of process, source reading/reuse, modification scope and three-file patch, then compatibility tests and cross-module integration check that loads config and logger and executes the queue-consuming function extracted from stats source, isolating distributed rank to local 0 without GPU deps; all conditions must pass for 1 point; check terminal conclusion then `result.json`, `源码阅读检查.json`, `regression.log`, `runtime.json`, `runtime.log`; modified sources in `modified-source/`, patch `deepinfer.patch`; problem 3 repeats this task and requires passing problem 2 first), plus the Course execution contract JSON: `{\"profile\": \"source\", \"editable\": [\"deepinfer/engine/stats_logger.py\", \"deepinfer/environ.py\", \"deepinfer/logger.py\"], \"required_full_reads\": [\"deepinfer/engine/stats_logger.py\", \"deepinfer/environ.py\", \"deepinfer/logger.py\"], \"verify_commands\": [[\"python\", \"-m\", \"pytest\", \"-q\"]], \"required_pages\": [], \"note_topics\": [], \"max_model_calls\": 20}` and the instruction to use update_plan before editing, run baseline checks, read required files with read_file, use returned `file_hash` as `expected_hash`, not reset a successful plan or repeat completed baseline checks, import allowed modules before use, and call final_answer only after current-file verification.\n   - The final user message asking for a summary of the conversation (text only, no tools).\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Edit `deepinfer/environ.py` (new min-bounded int-or-none factory + `DEEPINFER_LOG_MAX_MESSAGE_CHARS = EnvVar.int_or_none_min(32)` in the Logging section).\n   - Edit `deepinfer/logger.py` (keyword-only `max_message_chars` validation, truncation with `...<omitted>...`, clone-based non-mutating formatting, `keep_full_message is True` bypass, `_setup_logger` reading `envs.DEEPINFER_LOG_MAX_MESSAGE_CHARS`).\n   - Edit `deepinfer/engine/stats_logger.py` (`logger.info(m, extra={\"keep_full_message\": True})`).\n   - Run final full `python -m pytest -q` and ensure it passes.\n   - Generate `run.log`, `patch.diff` (three files), maintain `modified-source/`.\n   - Update plan statuses and call `final_answer` after verification.\n\n8. Current Work:\n   Immediately before the summary request, the assistant was trying to confirm the course tests' expectations for the new formatter argument by searching the repository for `max_message_chars` (two failed/blank attempts: `print(search_code(\"max_message_chars\", [\"tests\", \"deepinfer\"], 40))` and `hits = search_code(\"max_message_chars\", [\".\"], 40); print(hits)`), after having completed the baseline pytest (`rc=1`, \"50 failed, 10 passed in 2.37s\") and having all required mechanisms exposed (environ 3/3, logger 3/3, stats_logger 4/4) with full-read hashes registered. Course progress states `phase=edit`, `baseline_done=1`, `remaining source changes: deepinfer/engine/stats_logger.py, deepinfer/environ.py, deepinfer/logger.py`, `requests_left: 14`. Plan titles/order to preserve: \"Read required source files\" (doing), \"Run baseline pytest\" (todo → should be marked done), \"Edit environ.py, logger.py, stats_logger.py\" (todo), \"Run final pytest and produce artifacts\" (todo).\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Proceed directly to the first edits (no more exploratory test searching needed), applying scoped `replace_text` calls with the registered hashes: add `int_or_none_min` factory plus `DEEPINFER_LOG_MAX_MESSAGE_CHARS = EnvVar.int_or_none_min(32)` in environ.py, add `max_message_chars` + truncation logic and `max_message_chars=envs.DEEPINFER_LOG_MAX_MESSAGE_CHARS` in `_setup_logger` in logger.py, and change `logger.info(m)` to `logger.info(m, extra={\"keep_full_message\": True})` in stats_logger.py, then run `python -m pytest -q`. This is directly in line with the progress directive: \"Course progress before this request ... {\"phase\":\"edit\",\"next_requirement\":\"remaining source changes: deepinfer/engine/stats_logger.py, deepinfer/environ.py, deepinfer/logger.py\",\"remaining_count\":3 ... first_write_reading_required\":true ...}\" and the contract \"When progress says phase=edit, the initial reading and baseline are satisfied. Apply a scoped edit and verify.\"\n</summary>","reasoning_content":"Let me look at the current state. I have read the mechanisms. Now I need to make the edits. I have evidence for the relevant parts. Let me proceed to edit.\n\nFirst environ.py: add `_int_or_none_min` helper and the config item.\n\nLet me check `EnvVar.int_or_none` exists — yes. But I need min 32 validation and error message containing variable name (which is added by `__get__` wrapper: `f\"{self.name}: {e}\"`). So raising ValueError with message like \"must be >= 32\" gets prefixed with the name. Good.\n\nEmpty string: `int(\"\")` raises ValueError -> message \"invalid literal for int() with base 10: ''\" — wrapped with name. Good.\n\nNow write the descriptor:\n\n```python\n    @staticmethod\n    def int_or_none_min(min_value: int) -> EnvVar[int | None]:\n        def _init(v: str | None) -> int | None:\n            if v is None:\n                return None\n            value = int(v)\n            if value < min_value:\n                raise ValueError(f\"{value}, must be >= {min_value}\")\n            return value\n\n        return EnvVar(_init)\n```\n\nAnd config: `DEEPINFER_LOG_MAX_MESSAGE_CHARS = EnvVar.int_or_none_min(32)` in Logging section.\n\nNote: `from __future__ import annotations` is present, so `EnvVar[int | None]` annotation in factory is fine.\n\nNow logger.py formatter. Requirements:\n\n- `__init__(self, fmt, datefmt=None, high_precision=False, use_color=False, *, max_message_chars=None)`.\n- validate: None ok; bool not allowed; must be int >= 32.\n- format: apply args substitution first, then length count. Need access to record.getMessage() to compute message. But must not modify record.msg/args. `super().format(record)` sets `record.message = record.getMessage()` — actually `logging.Formatter.format` sets `record.message = record.getMessage()`. That's the standard behavior and allowed (it's what the original does too). The requirement says don't rewrite msg/args/exc_info/stack_info. Setting record.message is normal.\n\nSo plan: in format, first compute the truncated message and temporarily... hmm. The tricky part: `super().format(record)` formats using record.message and appends exc_info/stack_info. We want to truncate message after arg substitution but keep prefix and traceback intact.\n\nApproach:\n```python\ndef format(self, record):\n    max_chars = self.max_message_chars\n    if max_chars is not None and getattr(record, \"keep_full_message\", None) is not True:\n        try:\n            message = record.getMessage()\n        except Exception:\n            message = None\n        if message is not None and len(message) > max_chars:\n            truncated = _truncate_message(message, max_chars)\n            saved = (record.msg, record.args)\n            record.msg = truncated\n            record.args = ()\n            try:\n                s = self._format_with_prefix(record)\n            finally:\n                record.msg, record.args = saved\n            return s\n    return self._format_with_prefix(record)\n```\nWait — but modifying record.msg temporarily and restoring could be racy in threads, but the requirement says \"不能改写共享原记录的 msg、args、exc_info、stack_info\" — temporarily swapping during format and restoring... risky but functionally fine for a single-thread handler? Actually a shared LogRecord given to multiple handlers: handlers are called sequentially in `Logger.callHandlers`, so no concurrency for the same record within one thread. But cleaner: avoid mutating record at all by overriding record's message.\n\nBetter approach: `s = super().format(record)` gives full string with prefix and traceback. Instead, compute pieces ourselves? Requirement: \"沿用原有多行前缀、时间精度、颜色及异常处理\" — reusing existing logic is best.\n\nAlternative: don't pass record to super; instead compute:\n\nActually the simplest, non-mutating approach: build the formatted string via super().format(record) but make the message short. To do so without mutating the record, we can use `logging.makeLogRecord(record.__dict__)` copy? That copies and `record2.msg = truncated`, `record2.args = ()`. But exc_info contains traceback objects — fine. `formatter.format` caches exc_text on the record: `if record.exc_info ... record.exc_text`. With a copy, exc_text caching doesn't propagate to the original record — minor.\n\nHmm, but a copy via `logging.makeLogRecord(record.__dict__)`: makeLogRecord creates a LogRecord with `LogRecord(None, None, \"\", 0, \"\", (), None, None)` then `__dict__.update(dict)`. That works and is a documented approach.\n\nBut there's a subtlety: the truncation must happen after `%s` substitution — using record.getMessage() on the copy gives the same. Also multi-line prefix logic in our format uses `record.message`. Since `super().format()` sets `record.message` on the copy (the record we pass), and we use `record.message` in the newline logic — we should use the copy consistently.\n\nLet me write:\n\n```python\n_TRUNCATION_MARKER = \"...<omitted>...\"\n\ndef _truncate_message(message: str, max_chars: int) -> str:\n    marker = _TRUNCATION_MARKER\n    remaining = max_chars - len(marker)\n    if remaining <= 0:\n        return marker[:max_chars]\n    head_len = (remaining + 1) // 2\n    tail_len = remaining - head_len\n    tail = message[-tail_len:] if tail_len > 0 else \"\"\n    return message[:head_len] + marker + tail\n```\n\nCheck budget 32: remaining = 32-15 = 17; head = 9, tail = 8. ✓ (marker \"...<omitted>...\" — count: \"...\" 3 + \"<omitted>\" 9 + \"...\" 3 = 15 ✓).\n\nAlso multi-line: truncation happens before newline prefixing, so newlines in truncated message get prefixed properly. Fine.\n\nNow formatter:\n\n```python\nclass NewLineFormatter(logging.Formatter):\n    def __init__(self, fmt, datefmt=None, high_precision=False, use_color=False, *, max_message_chars=None):\n        super().__init__(fmt, datefmt)\n        self.high_precision = high_precision\n        self.use_color = use_color\n        if max_message_chars is not None:\n            if isinstance(max_message_chars, bool) or not isinstance(max_message_chars, int):\n                raise ValueError(f\"max_message_chars must be an int >= 32 or None, got {max_message_chars!r}\")\n            if max_message_chars < 32:\n                raise ValueError(f\"max_message_chars must be >= 32 or None, got {max_message_chars!r}\")\n        self.max_message_chars = max_message_chars\n```\n\nHmm, tests: \"test_invalid_budget[64] - TypeError: New...\" from the baseline run — that's an existing failing test expecting TypeError? Let me check the test to be sure about the expected exception type. Let me look at tests directory. The requirement says raise ValueError. But baseline test names showed \"est_invalid_budget[64] - TypeError: New\" meaning that param currently fails with TypeError because the kwarg isn't accepted. So tests expect ValueError eventually. Let me check tests to confirm which values are invalid (e.g. True, 31, \"64\"?). The spec says: 其他值须为大于等于32的整数，布尔值不算整数，否则抛出 ValueError. So non-int (e.g. float 64.0?) — spec says \"其他值须为大于等于32的整数\" — accept int >= 32. I'll raise ValueError for anything else, including float. Maybe tests pass 64.0 expecting ValueError or accepting? Safer to follow spec strictly: only int (non-bool) >= 32 accepted.\n\nNow format implementation:\n\n```python\n    def format(self, record: logging.LogRecord) -> str:\n        if self.max_message_chars is not None and getattr(record, \"keep_full_message\", None) is not True:\n            message = record.getMessage()\n            if len(message) > self.max_message_chars:\n                record = _copy_record_with_message(record, _truncate_message(message, self.max_message_chars))\n        msg = super().format(record)\n        ...\n```\n\n`record.getMessage()` could raise if args mismatched — original code also raises in super().format, so propagating is fine.\n\n`_copy_record_with_message`:\n```python\ndef _copy_record_with_message(record, message):\n    clone = logging.makeLogRecord(record.__dict__)\n    clone.msg = message\n    clone.args = ()\n    return clone\n```\nHmm but `record.__dict__` — makeLogRecord does `rv.__dict__.update(dict)`, which shares objects in dict (values) but dict itself is new. Then setting clone.msg doesn't affect record.msg. Good.\n\nWait, but exc_text caching: if the original record was already formatted by another handler (e.g. truncated one first then full)... The requirement says \"同一记录随后交给完整处理器，仍须保留完整消息\". Since we don't mutate the original, fine. Note also `record.message` on original gets set by full formatter later — fine.\n\nOne more subtlety: the clone's `exc_text` might be already set from a previous formatting — fine.\n\nAlso `record.message` attribute: after `super().format(clone)`, clone.message is the truncated message. Our newline logic uses `record.message` — but inside format we reassigned `record` to clone, so that's consistent. But careful: hyper-precision formatTime uses record.msecs — clone has it.\n\nNow the default init:\n\n```python\ndef _setup_logger() -> None:\n    global _default_handler\n    ...\n    fmt = NewLineFormatter(\n        _FORMAT,\n        datefmt=_DATE_FORMAT,\n        use_color=sys.stdout.isatty(),\n        max_message_chars=envs.DEEPINFER_LOG_MAX_MESSAGE_CHARS,\n    )\n```\n\nBut importing environ into logger: check for circular imports. environ.py imports only stdlib. logger.py importing `from deepinfer.environ import envs` — does environ import logger? No. Safe. Use `from deepinfer.environ import envs` at top of logger.py? Or local import inside `_setup_logger` to avoid cycles. Top-level is fine; but let me be careful about `deepinfer/__init__.py` importing logger... environ imports nothing from package, so no cycle.\n\nThen stats_logger: `logger.info(m, extra={\"keep_full_message\": True})`.\n\nLet me now check tests to confirm details before editing. Testing isn't required but useful — quick search on tests for \"max_message_chars\".\n\nLet me do a search and then edit. Actually, to save requests, let's search tests and read logger relevant lines in one action... I've already read logger 1-95, 110-174 (mechanisms exposed). Let me just search tests for expectations, then edit all three files in one action? Edits must be verified; I can do multiple replace_text calls in one action.\n\nLet me first search the tests."},"logprobs":null,"finish_reason":"stop"}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":10135,"completion_tokens":8806,"total_tokens":18941,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":4096},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":2459},"prompt_cache_hit_tokens":4096,"prompt_cache_miss_tokens":6039},"system_fingerprint":"bc19ba97cbe016479903222bb1578db6"}